From 27ba22cedae097472985385e181ae94414b79186 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Rebe?= <rene@exactco.de>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:59:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] target/i386/tcg: Inline and deduplicate entering MMX mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every MMX instruction called helper_enter_mmx.  As a helper without
call flags it forces all TCG globals to be synced to env and reloaded,
which made it the top host function for MMX code, e.g. 19% of OpenSSL
sha512 on i686.

Emit the fpstt/fptags stores inline instead, once per TB.  Only x87
instructions, EMMS, FXRSTOR and XRSTOR change fpstt/fptags within a
TB, so they reset the tracking.  Inline EMMS as well and drop the now
unused enter_mmx and emms helpers.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
